              <li class="lb-tabs-accordion-trigger">
               <div class="lb-txt-none lb-txt">
                Asynchronous Inference
               </div></li>
              <li tabindex="0" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="aws-element-6640d79d-00fb-4403-a3c8-0f5746098d32-tab-13" id="aws-element-6640d79d-00fb-4403-a3c8-0f5746098d32-panel-13" class="lb-tabs-content-item lb-comp-content-container lb-visibility-change">
               <div class="lb-content-wrapper">
                <div class="lb-rtxt">
                 <p><b>Amazon SageMaker Asynchronous Inference:</b> <br>
                   Amazon SageMaker Asynchronous Inference is a near-real time inference option that queues incoming requests and processes them asynchronously. Use this option when you need to process large payloads as the data arrives or run models that have long inference processing times and do not have sub-second latency requirements. You are charged for the type of instance you choose.</p>
                </div>
